server: a slot file carries the draft context's KV, and checkpoints keep the MTP head's h

A slot file held only the target context's state. The MTP draft keeps its
own KV over the prompt, so a slot restored on another server drafted over an
empty or another conversation's draft KV, and fewer drafts were accepted.
The save now appends the draft's sequence state after the checkpoints (magic
"QDFT"), and the restore loads it; a file without the block restores with
the draft KV cleared. A context checkpoint also keeps the MTP head's pending
hidden state, so the token re-read after a checkpoint restore is paired with
the right one. scripts/server-test-restore-draft.py checks that a restored
slot drafts exactly as the server that saved it.

